    "1 Pe",
    "1Pe"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-peter:5:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "The elders which are among you I exhort, who am also an elder, and a witness of the sufferings of Christ, and also a partaker of the glory that shall be revealed:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Peter 5:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-peter:5:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-peter:5:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Feed the flock of God which is among you, taking the oversight thereof, not by constraint, but willingly; not for filthy lucre, but of a ready mind;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Peter 5:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-peter:5:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-peter:5:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Neither as being lords over God’s heritage, but being ensamples to the flock.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Peter 5:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-peter:5:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-peter:5:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "And when the chief Shepherd shall appear, ye shall receive a crown of glory that fadeth not away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Peter 5:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-peter:5:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-peter:5:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Likewise, ye younger, submit yourselves unto the elder. Yea, all of you be subject one to another, and be clothed with humility: for God resisteth the proud, and giveth grace to the humble.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Peter 5:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-peter:5:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-peter:5:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Humble yourselves therefore under the mighty hand of God, that he may exalt you in due time:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Peter 5:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-peter:5:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-peter:5:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Casting all your care upon him; for he careth for you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Peter 5:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-peter:5:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-peter:5:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Peter 5:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-peter:5:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-peter:5:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Whom resist stedfast in the faith, knowing that the same afflictions are accomplished in your brethren that are in the world.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Peter 5:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-peter:5:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-peter:5:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "But the God of all grace, who hath called us unto his eternal glory by Christ Jesus, after that ye have suffered a while, make you perfect, stablish, strengthen, settle you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Peter 5:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-peter:5:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-peter:5:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "To him be glory and dominion for ever and ever. Amen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Peter 5:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-peter:5:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-peter:5:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "By Silvanus, a faithful brother unto you, as I suppose, I have written briefly, exhorting, and testifying that this is the true grace of God wherein ye stand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Peter 5:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-peter:5:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-peter:5:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "The church that is at Babylon, elected together with you, saluteth you; and so doth Marcus my son.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Peter 5:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-peter:5:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-peter:5:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Greet ye one another with a kiss of charity. Peace be with you all that are in Christ Jesus. Amen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Peter 5:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-peter:5:14"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
